236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 187 0 R
/T (The work of government is scrutinized through the electoral process. Businesses are held accountable through the actions of market forces. But despite directing vast resources toward public purposes and influencing the work of the vast nonprofit sector, philanthropy is subjected to comparatively few mechanisms for public scrutiny. By providing funding to the almost two million nonprofit organizations in the United States, philanthropic agencies make decisions that shape our educational, cultural, scientific, spiritual, health, and social service sectors. )
/E (The work of government is scrutinized through the electoral process. Businesses are held accountable through the actions of market forces. But despite directing vast resources toward public purposes and influencing the work of the vast nonprofit sector, philanthropy is subjected to comparatively few mechanisms for public scrutiny. By providing funding to the almost two million nonprofit organizations in the United States, philanthropic agencies make decisions that shape our educational, cultural, scientific, spiritual, health, and social service sectors. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
237 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 187 0 R
/T (At the Rockefeller Archive Center, we believe that philanthropy deserves the same level of thoughtful inquiry that governments and markets receive. Philanthropic institutions help determine which ideas are pursued, which problems receive attention, and which communities receive support. But how are those decisions made? Who sets the priorities? And what do we know about what has been effective and what has not? )
/E (At the Rockefeller Archive Center, we believe that philanthropy deserves the same level of thoughtful inquiry that governments and markets receive. Philanthropic institutions help determine which ideas are pursued, which problems receive attention, and which communities receive support. But how are those decisions made? Who sets the priorities? And what do we know about what has been effective and what has not? )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
238 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 187 0 R
/T (These are questions of growing importance, yet philanthropy remains an understudied field. Over the past 100 years, the contours of how philanthropy is structured and how it practices have evolved; understanding the work and influence of this enterprise draws on history, economics, politics, law, management, and public policy without fitting neatly into any one discipline, leaving significant gaps in research, public understanding, and professional practice. )
/E (These are questions of growing importance, yet philanthropy remains an understudied field. Over the past 100 years, the contours of how philanthropy is structured and how it practices have evolved; understanding the work and influence of this enterprise draws on history, economics, politics, law, management, and public policy without fitting neatly into any one discipline, leaving significant gaps in research, public understanding, and professional practice. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
239 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 187 0 R
/T (The Rockefeller Archive Center exists to help close those gaps. We preserve the historical record of philanthropy, make it available for independent research, advance archives and information management across the philanthropic sector, and support scholars and practitioners studying philanthropy's history and central and shared issues concerning contemporary practice. )
/E (The Rockefeller Archive Center exists to help close those gaps. We preserve the historical record of philanthropy, make it available for independent research, advance archives and information management across the philanthropic sector, and support scholars and practitioners studying philanthropy's history and central and shared issues concerning contemporary practice. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
240 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 187 0 R
/T (By building and sharing the evidence needed to understand philanthropy over time, we strengthen collective understanding, accountability, and informed decision-making. For philanthropy to serve the public good most effectively, evidence, reflection, and critical inquiry must be fostered to create useful knowledge. The archive remains foundational to this work. Over the next three years, the Rockefeller Archive Center will also use that foundation actively to convene inquiry, connect knowledge and perspectives, and bring what emerges into wider circulation and use. This 2026-2029 strategic plan outlines how we will strengthen the connections between the documentation, knowledge, and partnerships that make that inquiry possible. )
/E (By building and sharing the evidence needed to understand philanthropy over time, we strengthen collective understanding, accountability, and informed decision-making. For philanthropy to serve the public good most effectively, evidence, reflection, and critical inquiry must be fostered to create useful knowledge. The archive remains foundational to this work. Over the next three years, the Rockefeller Archive Center will also use that foundation actively to convene inquiry, connect knowledge and perspectives, and bring what emerges into wider circulation and use. This 2026-2029 strategic plan outlines how we will strengthen the connections between the documentation, knowledge, and partnerships that make that inquiry possible. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
