909 0 obj
<<
/Title (The work of government is scrutinized through the electoral process. Businesses are held accountable through the actions of market forces. But despite directing vast resources toward public purposes and influencing the work of the vast nonprofit sector, philanthropy is subjected to comparatively few mechanisms for public scrutiny. By providing funding to the almost two million nonprofit organizations in the United States, philanthropic agencies make decisions that shape our educational, cultural, scientific, spiritual, health, and social service sectors.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 814 0 R
/Next 987 0 R
>>
endobj
910 0 obj
<<
/Title (By building and sharing the evidence needed to understand philanthropy over time, we strengthen collective understanding, accountability, and informed decision-making. For philanthropy to serve the public good most effectively, evidence, reflection, and critical inquiry must be fostered to create useful knowledge. The archive remains foundational to this work. Over the next three years, the Rockefeller Archive Center will also use that foundation actively to convene inquiry, connect knowledge and perspectives, and bring what emerges into wider circulation and use. This 2026-2029 strategic plan outlines how we will strengthen the connections between the documentation, knowledge, and partnerships that make that inquiry possible.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 814 0 R
/Prev 988 0 R
>>
endobj
