/Title (These are questions of growing importance, yet philanthropy remains an understudied field. Over the past 100 years, the contours of how philanthropy is structured and how it practices have evolved; understanding the work and influence of this enterprise draws on history, economics, politics, law, management, and public policy without fitting neatly into any one discipline, leaving significant gaps in research, public understanding, and professional practice.)
